From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ai_re <ai_re@localhost>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 22/26] pci: add the Annapurna Labs Alpine V2 external PCIe
 root complex

Root complex driver for the Alpine V2 external PCIe ports, bound to the
node mainline Linux pcie-al uses ("amazon,al-alpine-v2-pcie": config,
controller and dbi regs). The port is brought up on Annapurna's PCIe HAL
3.4 (drivers/pci/al_pcie/al_hal_*, copied unmodified from the MikroTik
GPL Linux 5.6.3 source drop, drivers/soc/alpine/HAL: the Annapurna files
are triple-licensed and used under GPL-2.0; the Amazon 2017 files carry
no licence of their own and are distributed as part of that GPL kernel
source) plus U-Boot platform shims.

al_init_pcie_rc.c is the RC path of the vendor's al_init_pcie() service
with the parameters the factory U-Boot 2.60.4 passes for an external
port: teardown of a running port (link stop, memory shutdown, port
disable), port enable/disable/enable around mode RC, max lanes and one
PF, port config (AXI snoop on, slave error response on, the factory's
Gen3 EQ table, link speed and lanes from the DT), link start, link-up
wait and the 48 ms wait for full speed; on failure the vendor teardown.
No SerDes iCal: the factory passes no SerDes groups for these ports.

Probe: a link the firmware already trained is kept (chainloaded after
the vendor U-Boot); a port without a link is initialised if the DT gives
amazon,link-gen and amazon,link-lanes (started by al-boot stage3 instead
of the vendor U-Boot), rev 3 units only. The root port's header is the
DesignWare core (dbi); downstream config cycles go through the config
window with the target bus register, secondary bus 1, subordinate 0xff,
as pcie-al does; one device on the link bus. iATU region 0 maps the
memory window 1:1, as Linux dwc does.

With the AXI slave error response on, a failed downstream config read
(CRS, UR) is an asynchronous SError on this SoC. Like the factory U-Boot,
the driver drains it after each downstream access (HCR_EL2.AMO + a
vector table whose SError entry returns), returns all ones, and retries a
vendor ID read while the device answers CRS (30 s, ctrl-c).

"alpcie status" shows port, link and unit registers; "alpcie reinit"
removes the bus, runs the full init from a torn-down port and
enumerates again, so a RAM test after the factory init proves this init.

Scope: alpine-v2.
